cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  GenomeForge: a whole-genome germline joint-calling pipeline
  (FASTQ → annotated, QC'd cohort callset)
message: If you use GenomeForge, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Adu
    given-names: Bright
    affiliation: "Genomics and Bioinformatics Core Facility, Noguchi Memorial Institute for Medical Research, University of Ghana, Legon, Ghana"
abstract: >-
  GenomeForge is a reusable Nextflow (DSL2) pipeline for whole-genome germline
  analysis on SLURM clusters. It takes paired-end Illumina FASTQs in any lane,
  flowcell or library layout through per-lane bwa-mem2 alignment, duplicate
  marking, base-quality recalibration, scattered HaplotypeCaller gVCF calling,
  GenomicsDB joint genotyping, VQSR, normalisation, dbSNP/gnomAD/ClinVar/VEP
  annotation and cohort QC (relatedness, sex, contamination, PCA, MultiQC). It
  runs on the CallForge container images and reference bundle and is the
  whole-genome sibling of the CallForge targeted-panel pipeline.
keywords:
  - whole-genome sequencing
  - germline variant calling
  - joint genotyping
  - GATK
  - nextflow
  - bioinformatics
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-20
repository-code: https://github.com/aduton1000/genomeforge
references:
  - type: software
    title: "CallForge: a targeted-capture germline analysis pipeline"
    notes: "Sibling pipeline; GenomeForge reuses its container images and reference bundle."
